IBM CLOUD CODE ENGINE DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION & STATUS
================================================================================
Status: Environment-Restricted (IBM Cloud Code Engine CLI & Cloud Account Required)

Target Code Engine Deployed URL Format:
https://dealership-django.<random-hash>.<region>.codeengine.appdomain.cloud/

Deployment Manifests & Container Files Prepared in Repository:
- server/Dockerfile (Python 3.11 Slim, Gunicorn WSGI production server)
- server/entrypoint.sh (Auto-migrations and static files collection)
- docker-compose.yml (Orchestrates Django, Node/Express, MongoDB, Sentiment service)

Commands to deploy directly to IBM Cloud Code Engine once credentials are authenticated:
1. ibmcloud login -u <YOUR_IBM_EMAIL> --sso
2. ibmcloud target -g Default -r us-south
3. ibmcloud ce project create --name dealership-portal
4. ibmcloud ce project select --name dealership-portal
5. ibmcloud ce application create --name dealership-django \
     --build-source ./server \
     --port 8000 \
     --env backend_url=http://dealership-node:3030 \
     --env sentiment_analyzer_url=http://dealership-sentiment:5050/ \
     --min-scale 1 --max-scale 3
6. ibmcloud ce application get --name dealership-django --output url
